ring 0.17.14 for thumbv7em-none-eabihf (the nRF52840), used by nrf52840/
through [patch.crates-io]; scripts/vendor-ring.sh applies it to a copy of the
crate in .tools/ring-nrf. Not proposed upstream. Same license as ring.

- build.rs: assemble ring's 32-bit ARM perlasm (linux32 flavour) for
  target_os = "none" too, so SHA-2, AES and GHASH keep their assembly, but
  skip x25519-asm-arm.S and poly1305_arm_asm.S: both are NEON in ARM state,
  which a Thumb-only Cortex-M4 can neither assemble nor run.
- src/aead/poly1305.rs, ffi_arm_neon.rs: leave the NEON Poly1305 out on
  target_os = "none" to match (ring picks it only after a runtime NEON check,
  which never passes there, but the call would still need the symbol).

diff -ruN a/build.rs b/build.rs
--- a/build.rs	2026-11-12 02:15:55.638734665 -0800
+++ b/build.rs	2026-11-12 02:15:58.711441730 -0800
@@ -195,6 +195,14 @@
         arch: ARM,
         perlasm_format: "linux32",
     },
+    // Bare-metal Thumb-2 (thumbv7m/thumbv7em): the same ARMv4/ARMv7 perlasm,
+    // which assembles as Thumb-2 under `__thumb2__`; its NEON paths are
+    // never selected without NEON.
+    AsmTarget {
+        oss: &["none"],
+        arch: ARM,
+        perlasm_format: "linux32",
+    },
     AsmTarget {
         oss: APPLE_ABI,
         arch: AARCH64,
@@ -460,6 +468,17 @@
                 {
                     return false;
                 }
+                // x25519-asm-arm.S and poly1305_arm_asm.S are NEON in ARM
+                // state, which a Thumb-only core can neither assemble nor
+                // run; ring calls the first only on Linux and Android, and
+                // the second not on bare metal (src/aead/poly1305.rs).
+                if target.arch == ARM
+                    && target.os == "none"
+                    && (p.ends_with("crypto/curve25519/asm/x25519-asm-arm.S")
+                        || p.ends_with("crypto/poly1305/poly1305_arm_asm.S"))
+                {
+                    return false;
+                }
             }
             true
         })
